-- The data-receiver twin of `admitted-set-rigid-receiver-rejected`: `hub` re-exports
-- two unrelated `mth : a -> a`, from `IA` (`T (n + 1)`) and `IB` (`T (n * 10)`), both
-- with an impl at `T`.  Inside `wrap` the receiver is the rigid `x`, so no
-- declaration's impl query can be asked and the two are not shown to agree.
-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS.md S2-DECL (d) over the admitted set (ruled 2026-10-14): the
-- located reject `T-AMBIGUOUS-METHOD` at `mth` in `wrap`, exit 1 on every verb, in
-- either hub order (`swapped.mdk`).  Never 4 or 30 (the two hub orders' `run` values
-- while the occurrence kept no route), nor a run-time `E-AMBIGUOUS-DISPATCH`.
import hub.{IA, IB, mth}
import t.{T(..)}

wrap : x -> x
wrap v = mth v

main = match wrap (T 3)
  T n => println n
